        "original_id": "5acf935e-8ae8-5045-9e6c-c86416236256",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Kevin Sinfield\n- Places: AJ Bell Stadium, Salford City Stadium, Barton-upon-Irwell, Eccles, Salford, England\n- Organizations: Leeds, Salford Red Devils\n- Awards: Lance Todd Trophy, Harry Sunderland Trophy, Golden Boot\n- Topics: Super League, Challenge Cup\n\nFacts:\n- Kevin Sinfield played his entire professional career with Leeds.\n- Kevin Sinfield captained Leeds to seven Super League championships and two Challenge Cup successes.\n- Kevin Sinfield won the Lance Todd Trophy in 2005.\n- Kevin Sinfield won the Harry Sunderland Trophy in 2009 and 2012.\n- Kevin Sinfield won the Golden Boot in 2012 and was one of only four British-based players to do so.\n- The Lance Todd Trophy is presented at a celebratory dinner at the AJ Bell Stadium, the home of the Salford Red Devils.\n- Salford City Stadium is referred to as the AJ Bell Stadium for sponsorship purposes.\n- Salford City Stadium is a rugby stadium in Barton-upon-Irwell, Eccles, Salford, England.",
